ou were doing a  particular job you would look at the  molds again you would look at you know  beards or things again if something  could be improved upon we were on a  series where you could do that  hairstylist friend of mine a number of  years ago said  don't match if you can make it better  another question  this is for the two makeup artists from  europe do you see anything  in general any differences between  makeup artistry training or working in  europe as compared to the united states  i think  there's so much uh  mix between europe and the states that  all the skills  intermingle and everybody learns from  everybody else so not really you don't  see too much for difference  i could say that um in england  there isn't a structured teaching scheme  um there's lots of colleges and lots of  private schools you can go to and part  with a lot of money some of them are  very good some aren't um  i don't know because i've never worked  over here  on a major movie i don't know how it's  structured here but it does seem to me  that to work on movies over here it is  tougher  um  at home  if i want to hire somebody  they can come and see me show me their  portfolio and their last job could have  been  you know in a supermarket and we can  hire them  we have there we have a union  i what's it called  exactly um  they used to have tests and all of that  kind of thing um but  it just frittered away  which does mean in europe there are lots  of people who say they're makeup artists  or hairdressers and there's lots of very  good ones there's also a lot of people  who have no right to the name whatsoever  and there is no policing of it  it's a little bit different in ireland  you either are a hair person or a makeup  person and it's quite rigid people stick  to that i think  our union's a little bit stronger but  we don't have um exams it's all based on  the level of experience you acquire as  time goes on whether you upgrade to the  next level or not  but they have you h